const next = counter + 1;
await db.query('UPDATE counters SET counter = $1 WHERE id = $2', [next, id]);
```

Two requests can read the same value before either updates it.

## Use an atomic PostgreSQL update

Let PostgreSQL increment and return the value in one statement:

```sql
UPDATE counters
SET value = value + 1
WHERE id = $1
RETURNING value;
```

With `node-postgres`:

```js
