    res.json({ value: result.rows[0].value });
  } catch (err) {
    next(err);
  }
});
```

PostgreSQL locks the affected row while updating it. Concurrent updates to the same row are serialized, so each request receives a different incremented value.

## If the counter row might not exist

Use an atomic upsert:

```js
