  `SELECT nextval('api_counter_seq') AS value`
);

res.json({ value: result.rows[0].value });
```

Sequence values are concurrency-safe and unique, though gaps are possible if requests fail or transactions roll back.

Avoid fixing this with only a JavaScript mutex: it will not protect you once the API runs in multiple Node.js processes or containers. Put the concurrency control in PostgreSQL.

